 faqs:[{question:'What should a Bengali biodata focus on?',answer:'A clear personal profile, family background, education, career, values and a safe contact method form a strong base.'},{question:'Should I add community or lineage details?',answer:'Only if your family considers them relevant. They should remain optional.'},{question:'How long should the about section be?',answer:'A short paragraph is usually enough. Focus on personality, interests and values that help someone start a conversation.'},{question:'Can the biodata be shared privately?',answer:'Yes. Keep the first version limited to information you are comfortable forwarding through relatives.'}],
