 faqs:[{question:'Should a Jain biodata mention sect?',answer:'It can if the family considers it relevant. Use the exact family terminology and keep the field optional.'},{question:'Should I assume dietary preferences?',answer:'No. If diet matters to the match, state the person’s actual preference directly.'},{question:'Is gotra required?',answer:'Not universally. Include it when the family uses it and has verified the information.'},{question:'How should religious details be written?',answer:'Use factual, respectful language describing the person or family rather than making broad claims about all Jains.'}],
