 faqs:[{question:'Should a Muslim biodata include sect?',answer:'Only if the family considers it relevant. Use the family’s own terminology and keep the field optional.'},{question:'Should religious practice be described?',answer:'It can be, especially if it affects compatibility, but it should describe the individual rather than make universal claims.'},{question:'What should an NRI Muslim biodata include?',answer:'Country, city, occupation and broad residency status are useful; avoid publishing immigration document numbers.'},{question:'How can expectations remain respectful?',answer:'Describe values and practical preferences clearly while avoiding a long list of demands or assumptions about the other family.'}],
